cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: Configuration-Stable PairHMM Score Reduction
version: 1.0.0
type: software
abstract: Measured configuration stability of a GATK-style PairHMM aggregate haplotype-score reduction under a canonical compensated policy. Unordered parallel reduction changed the haplotype-score fingerprint with thread count or GPU block size. The canonical policy did not, on the recorded workloads. This repository publishes the methods note and a closed Linux evaluation binary. It does not publish source code and does not license the LuxiEdge engine.
